* The menu only lists, marks, copies and deletes. D/C change marks; X
* performs the selected operations through DSR calls, not direct EEPROM edits.
* UBF1 file manager. DSR work goes through the console scanner.
* VDP: catalog PAB0040, copy PABs1200/1240, marks1300, message1340,
* directory1400, data2000. Hide the screen while the catalog PAB is visible.
* Included in the service GROM; the single header links both entry points.
* Included by ube1.gpl; this file includes basic-cat.gpl at its end.
* CATDRAW calls shared CATREADDIR/CATTABLE; numeric display helpers here
* are also used by BASIC CAT. Removing either UI source needs refactoring.
* CATSOURCE/CATDEST call the console DSR scanner, which finds UBE1 or the
* user's destination device. External copies need that device's own DSR.
PREFIXLEN EQU 5
CATPROG DATA 0,CATSTART
       STRI 'SAVED GAMES'
* Own the keyboard mode instead of inheriting the title scanner's default.
* Use the console's compact upper-case font, at the ASCII 32 pattern address.
CATSTART MOVE 1,G@CATBLANK,#1
       ST 3,@>8374
       DST >0900,@>834A
       CALL >0018
       MOVE 16,G@CATZERO,V@>1300
       MOVE 32,G@CATSPACES,V@>1340
       DCLR @>832A
       DST 96,@>8334
* Startup only: drain keys held while selecting the menu. CATDRAW must not
* re-arm this after an action or a copy prompt.
       ST 1,@>833A
       DCLR @>6000
CATDRAW MOVE 1,G@CATBLANK,#1
       ALL 32
       BACK 4
       MOVE CATHEAD-CATTITLE,G@CATTITLE,V@5
       MOVE 32,V@>1340,V@608
       CLR @>833D
       DST >1400,@>8332
       CALL CATREADDIR
* Clear the entire temporary PAB, including the opcode at column zero.
* Also needed on the directory-error path, which does not draw a header.
       MOVE 16,G@CATSPACES,V@>40
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATNOMAP
       CLR @>833C
       MOVE CATPREFIX-CATHEAD,G@CATHEAD,V@65
       DST >1420,@>8332
       DST 97,@>8320
       CALL CATTABLE
       MOVE CATMAPERR-CATCOUNTTEXT,G@CATCOUNTTEXT,V@33
       ST V@>1409,@>8324
       CALL CATDEC
       MOVE 2,@>8326,V@33
       ST V@>1407,@>8324
       CALL CATDEC
       MOVE 3,@>8325,V@49
       ST >3E,V*>8334
       B CATFOOTER
CATNOMAP ST 1,@>833C
       MOVE CATKEY1-CATMAPERR,G@CATMAPERR,V@161
CATFOOTER MOVE CATKEY2-CATKEY1,G@CATKEY1,V@673
       MOVE CATKEY3-CATKEY2,G@CATKEY2,V@705
       MOVE CATKEYEND-CATKEY3,G@CATKEY3,V@746
       MOVE 1,G@CATSHOW,#1
CATWAIT CZ @>833A
       BS CATKEY
       SCAN
       CEQ >FF,@>8375
       BR CATWAIT
       CLR @>833A
CATKEY SCAN
       BR CATWAIT
       CEQ 13,@>8375
       BS CATQUIT
       CEQ 11,@>8375
       BS CATUP
       CEQ >45,@>8375
       BS CATUP
       CEQ 10,@>8375
       BS CATDOWN
       CEQ >53,@>8375
       BS CATDOWN
       CEQ >44,@>8375
       BS CATMARK
       CEQ >43,@>8375
       BS CATMARK
       CEQ >58,@>8375
       BS CATEXEC
       B CATWAIT
CATQUIT EXIT
CATUP  DCZ @>832A
       BS CATWAIT
       ST >20,V*>8334
       DDEC @>832A
       DSUB 32,@>8334
       ST >3E,V*>8334
       B CATWAIT
CATDOWN DCEQ 15,@>832A
       BS CATWAIT
       ST >20,V*>8334
       DINC @>832A
       DADD 32,@>8334
       ST >3E,V*>8334
       B CATWAIT
CATMARK CZ @>833C
       BR CATWAIT
       ST @>8375,@>8339
       ST @>832B,@>8324
       CALL CATRECORD
       CZ V*>8350
       BS CATWAIT
       DST >1300,@>832C
       DADD @>832A,@>832C
       CEQ @>8339,V*>832C
       BS CATUNMARK
       ST @>8339,V*>832C
       DST @>8334,@>8328
       DADD 30,@>8328
       ST @>8339,V*>8328
       B CATWAIT
CATUNMARK CLR V*>832C
       DST @>8334,@>8328
       DADD 30,@>8328
       ST >20,V*>8328
       B CATWAIT
* Execute the marks only when X is pressed. Keep a failed operation's
* mark so the user can see which action did not finish.
CATEXEC CZ @>833C
       BR CATWAIT
       CLR @>832E
       MOVE 32,G@CATSPACES,V@>1340
CATBATCH DCLR @>832C
       ST @>832E,@>832D
       DADD >1300,@>832C
       ST V*>832C,@>8339
       CZ @>8339
       BS CATBNEXT
       ST @>832E,@>8324
       CALL CATRECORD
       CZ V*>8350
       BS CATBCLEAR
       CEQ >44,@>8339
       BR CATBCOPY
       CALL CATDELETE
       B CATRESULT
CATBCOPY CALL CATCOPY
CATRESULT CZ @>835F
       BR CATDRAW
CATBCLEAR DCLR @>832C
       ST @>832E,@>832D
       DADD >1300,@>832C
       CLR V*>832C
CATBNEXT INC @>832E
       CEQ 16,@>832E
       BR CATBATCH
       MOVE CATDONEEND-CATDONE,G@CATDONE,V@>1340
       B CATDRAW
* Slot number in >8324; returns VDP directory entry >8350.
CATRECORD DST >1420,@>8350
CATRECLP CZ @>8324
       BS CATRECRET
       DADD 32,@>8350
       DEC @>8324
       B CATRECLP
CATRECRET RTN
* Construct the source PAB from the validated directory entry.
CATPAB MOVE 16,G@CATZERO,V@>1200
       DST >2000,V@>1202
       DST V@12(@>50),V@>1206
       ST V@10(@>50),@>8336
       ST V@21(@>50),@>8337
       MOVE 5,G@CATPREFIX,V@>120A
       MOVE 10,V*>8350,V@>120F
       DST 10,@>8352
CATPTRIM CEQ 32,V@>120E(@>52)
       BR CATPNAME
       DDEC @>8352
       B CATPTRIM
CATPNAME ADD 5,@>8353
       ST @>8353,V@>1209
       RTN
CATDELETE CALL CATPAB
       ST 7,V@>1200
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CZ @>835F
       BS CATDELRET
       MOVE CATERRC-CATERRD,G@CATERRD,V@>1340
CATDELRET RTN
CATCOPY CALL CATPAB
       MOVE 16,G@CATZERO,V@>1240
       DST >2000,V@>1242
       ALL 32
       MOVE CATCOPYTITLEEND-CATCOPYTITLE,G@CATCOPYTITLE,V@65
       MOVE PREFIXLEN+10,V@>120A,V@129
       MOVE CATINPUTHELP-CATPROMPT,G@CATPROMPT,V@193
       MOVE CATCOPYTITLE-CATINPUTHELP,G@CATINPUTHELP,V@353
       CLR @>833B
       DST 257,@>8332
CATINPUT SCAN
       BR CATINPUT
       CEQ 13,@>8375
       BS CATCONFIRM
       CEQ 8,@>8375
       BS CATBACK
       CH 31,@>8375
       BR CATINPUT
       CH 95,@>8375
       BS CATINPUT
       CH 29,@>833B
       BS CATINPUT
       DCLR @>8354
       ST @>833B,@>8355
       ST @>8375,V@>124A(@>54)
       ST @>8375,V*>8332
       INC @>833B
       DINC @>8332
       B CATINPUT
CATBACK CZ @>833B
       BS CATINPUT
       DEC @>833B
       DDEC @>8332
       ST >20,V*>8332
       B CATINPUT
* Copy routing: UBE1 destinations use private CLONE (opcode 12), keeping
* the native file attributes. Other devices use PROGRAM LOAD/SAVE or
* record OPEN/READ/WRITE/CLOSE, according to the source file type.
CATCONFIRM CZ @>833B
       BS CATCOPYCANCEL
       ST @>833B,V@>1249
       DCEQ >5542,V@>124A
       BR CATEXTERNAL
       DCEQ >4531,V@>124C
       BR CATEXTERNAL
       CEQ >2E,V@>124E
       BR CATEXTERNAL
       ST 12,V@>1200
       DST >1249,V@>1202
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYERR
       RTN
CATEXTERNAL
       ST @>8336,@>835F
       AND 1,@>835F
       CZ @>835F
       BS CATCOPYRECORDS
       ST 5,V@>1200
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYERR
       ST 6,V@>1240
       DST V@>1206,V@>1246
       CALL CATDEST
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYERR
       RTN
CATCOPYRECORDS ST @>8336,@>835F
       AND >80,@>835F
       SRL 3,@>835F
       ST @>8336,@>835E
       AND 2,@>835E
       SLL 2,@>835E
       OR @>835E,@>835F
       ST @>835F,V@>1201
       ST @>835F,V@>1241
       OR 4,V@>1201
       OR 2,V@>1241
       ST @>8337,V@>1204
       ST @>8337,V@>1244
       DCLR V@>1206
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYERR
       CALL CATDEST
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCLOSESOURCE
CATCOPYLOOP ST 2,V@>1200
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CEQ >A0,@>835F
       BS CATCOPYEND
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYABORT
       ST V@>1205,V@>1245
       ST 3,V@>1240
       CALL CATDEST
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYABORT
       B CATCOPYLOOP
CATCOPYEND ST 1,V@>1240
       CALL CATDEST
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYABORT
       ST 1,V@>1200
       CALL CATSOURCE
       CZ @>835F
       BR CATCOPYERR
       RTN
CATCOPYABORT ST 1,V@>1240
       DCEQ >5542,V@>124A
       BR CATCOPYCLEAN
       DCEQ >4531,V@>124C
       BR CATCOPYCLEAN
       ST 10,V@>1240
CATCOPYCLEAN CALL CATDEST
CATCLOSESOURCE ST 1,V@>1200
       CALL CATSOURCE
       B CATCOPYERR
CATSOURCE DST >1209,@>8356
       CALL >0010
       BYTE >08
       BS CATIOFAIL
       ST V@>1201,@>835F
       AND >E0,@>835F
       RTN
CATDEST DST >1249,@>8356
       CALL >0010
       BYTE >08
       BS CATIOFAIL
       ST V@>1241,@>835F
       AND >E0,@>835F
       RTN
CATIOFAIL ST >C0,@>835F
       RTN

CATCOPYCANCEL MOVE CATDONE-CATCANCEL,G@CATCANCEL,V@>1340
       ST 1,@>835F
       RTN
CATCOPYERR CEQ >80,@>835F
       BR CATCOPYOTHER
       MOVE CATFULLEND-CATFULLERR,G@CATFULLERR,V@>1340
       B CATCOPYFAILED
CATCOPYOTHER CEQ >20,@>835F
       BR CATCOPYGENERIC
       MOVE CATPROTEND-CATPROTERR,G@CATPROTERR,V@>1340
       B CATCOPYFAILED
CATCOPYGENERIC MOVE CATCANCEL-CATERRC,G@CATERRC,V@>1340
CATCOPYFAILED
       ST 1,@>835F
       RTN
* Decimal word >8324->four ASCII digits >8325..>8328.
CATWORD DST @>8324,@>835C
       ST >30,@>8325
CATTHOU DCH 999,@>835C
       BR CATHUND
       DSUB 1000,@>835C
       INC @>8325
       B CATTHOU
CATHUND ST >30,@>8326
CATHLP DCH 99,@>835C
       BR CATWTENS
       DSUB 100,@>835C
       INC @>8326
       B CATHLP
CATWTENS ST >30,@>8327
CATWTLP DCH 9,@>835C
       BR CATWONES
       DSUB 10,@>835C
       INC @>8327
       B CATWTLP
CATWONES ST >30,@>8328
       ADD @>835D,@>8328
       RTN
* Decimal byte >8324 -> three ASCII digits >8325->8327.
CATDEC ST @>8324,@>8325
       CLR @>8324
       CALL CATWORD
       MOVE 3,@>8326,@>8325
       RTN
CATTITLE TEXT 'UBE1 FILE MANAGER'
CATHEAD TEXT 'FILE       TYPE         BYTES *'
CATPREFIX TEXT 'UBE1.'
CATCOUNTTEXT TEXT '00 FILES        000 BLOCKS FREE'
CATMAPERR TEXT 'UBE1 STORAGE NOT READY'
CATKEY1 TEXT 'E/S:MOVE            ENTER:EXIT'
CATKEY2 TEXT 'D:MARK DELETE      C:MARK COPY'
CATKEY3 TEXT 'X:DO MARKED'
CATKEYEND
CATERRD TEXT 'DELETE FAILED - MARK KEPT'
CATERRC TEXT 'COPY FAILED - MARK KEPT'
CATCANCEL TEXT 'COPY CANCELED - MARK KEPT'
CATDONE TEXT 'DONE - MARKED ACTIONS COMPLETED'
CATDONEEND
CATFULLERR TEXT 'NO SPACE - OLD FILE RETAINED'
CATFULLEND
CATPROTERR TEXT 'PROTECTED - MARK KEPT'
CATPROTEND
CATPROMPT TEXT 'DESTINATION (E.G. DSK1.PIRATE):'
CATINPUTHELP TEXT 'ENTER TO COPY; BLANK TO CANCEL'
CATCOPYTITLE TEXT 'COPY SAVE'
CATCOPYTITLEEND
CATZERO EQU ZEROS
CATSPACES TEXT '                                '
* Graphics mode, interrupts on; console preserves the VDP memory-size bit.
CATBLANK BYTE >20
CATSHOW BYTE >60
       COPY 'basic-cat.gpl'
